[32m+[m[32m**ADR-023 — Payment Ownership Reconciliation: Payments owns the gateway transaction, Billing owns the ledger entry (2026-09-08)**[m
[32m+[m[32m- Status: **PROPOSED**[m
[32m+[m[32m- Date: 2026-09-08[m
[32m+[m[32m- Context: The same audit found BILLING independently declaring[m
[32m+[m[32m  `Payment`/`RecordPayment`/`PaymentReceived` with direct payment-gateway[m
[32m+[m[32m  integration, while PAYMENTS independently declared[m
[32m+[m[32m  `PaymentTransaction`/`RefundTransaction`/`CapturePayment`/`IssueRefund`/[m
[32m+[m[32m  `PaymentCaptured` with its own direct gateway integration, idempotency[m
[32m+[m[32m  handling, and PCI DSS tokenization detail BILLING lacked entirely. A[m
[32m+[m[32m  prior session pass had edited only `05`'s workflow narrative to assume[m
[32m+[m[32m  a delegation to Payments, without correcting `03`'s BILLING entry —[m
[32m+[m[32m  meaning the underlying domain-map conflict was never actually[m
[32m+[m[32m  resolved, only masked in one downstream document. Recorded as ACR-5[m
[32m+[m[32m  (originally surfaced as a Cloud #2-reported finding, independently[m
[32m+[m[32m  re-verified against `03` directly before this ADR was written).[m
[32m+[m[32m- Decision: The repository owner selected Option C — a two-layer split,[m
[32m+[m[32m  not a full removal of `Payment` from Billing. PAYMENTS owns[m
[32m+[m[32m  `PaymentTransaction`, `RefundTransaction`, all gateway interaction,[m
[32m+[m[32m  idempotency, and tokenization — the transaction lifecycle in full.[m
[32m+[m[32m  BILLING keeps `Payment` but redefined as a ledger/accounting posting[m
[32m+[m[32m  record only; `PaymentTransaction` and `Payment` are explicitly[m
[32m+[m[32m  declared distinct objects. PAYMENTS emits `PaymentCaptured`; BILLING[m
[32m+[m[32m  consumes that event and performs its own ledger posting[m
[32m+[m[32m  (`RecordPayment`) in reaction — Billing is explicitly prohibited from[m
[32m+[m[32m  being gateway-facing or a second source of truth for the transaction.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Decision Provenance: This resolution (Option C, the two-layer split)[m
[32m+[m[32m  was explicitly directed by the repository owner in the governing[m
[32m+[m[32m  project conversation for this repository. This is a record of that[m
[32m+[m[32m  direction, not a formal ADR approval — Status remains PROPOSED until[m
[32m+[m[32m  the repository owner (or whatever future mechanism[m
[32m+[m[32m  `DECISION-AUTHORITY.md` establishes) formally approves it through[m
[32m+[m[32m  this document's own change process.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Rationale: This preserves Billing's existing ledger/accounting[m
[32m+[m[32m  vocabulary (avoiding a wholesale rewrite of its financial-ledger[m
[32m+[m[32m  framing) while eliminating the actual defect — two domains each[m
[32m+[m[32m  claiming direct gateway ownership. Workflow #9 (Billing) in `05` was[m
[32m+[m[32m  updated to encode the Payments transaction boundary explicitly —[m
[32m+[m[32m  `PaymentCaptured` → Billing ledger posting, and the removal of[m
[32m+[m[32m  Billing's direct gateway role — since the workflow's prior text had[m
[32m+[m[32m  already (prematurely, and without this precise boundary) assumed some[m
[32m+[m[32m  form of Payments delegation.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Consequences: `03-MASTER-DOMAIN-MAP.md`'s BILLING and PAYMENTS entries[m
[32m+[m[32m  updated; `05-MASTER-WORKFLOW-MAP.md` workflow #9 (Billing) updated to[m
[32m+[m[32m  match the ledger/transaction split precisely (previously it read as[m
